  "_notes": [
    "What an Unknown-reputation Common recruit arrives wearing.",
    "CANON: starting gear carries AC only. No HP, Power or Mana on any piece.",
    "CANON: no weapon, off-hand or trinket — a Common recruit shows up unarmed.",
    "NAME COLLISION, deliberate (docs/09 §5): 'Worn Leggings' is canon for both",
    "Warrior/Bard at 2 AC and the three healers at 1 AC. Same name, two different",
    "items. They are kept as separate entries disambiguated by family, exactly as",
    "docs/09 proposes, so the collision never reaches the data layer as one item.",
    "'Worn Trousers' (Monk, and Mage/Wizard) and 'Old Sandals' (Monk, and healers)",
    "collide the same way but agree on stats.",
    "Where canon gives two classes in one family different named pieces, the ID",
    "carries a VARIANT suffix per docs/09 §12.1.",
    "starting_sets is the contract the recruiter uses: class key -> item ids."
  ],

